From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:40:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 108/115] Signed div/mod by powers of 2 of a non-negative
 dividend become shr/and

A signed x div 2^k needs a correction for negative x before the shift (and
x mod 2^k one before the mask). optrange computes the range of the dividend
from constants, the storage range of types, for loop counters (in the body
of "for c := s to e", c lies between the smallest s and the largest e) and
temps (the union of what is assigned to them, each in the context of its
loops), through additions, subtractions and multiplications that cannot
overflow; with a non-negative dividend the division is a shr, the modulo an
and. Runs before the for loops become while loops.
spectralnorm: (i+j)*(i+j+1) div 2 in eval_A (inner loop 19 -> 16
instructions); tests/test/opt/tnonnegdiv1.pp.
